# text = A noble Peer , whose practised talents have already benefited the nation , and who , on vacating his seat in the Cabinet , was elevated in the Peerage , is reported as having had certain overtures made him , the nature of which may be conceived , but which , under present circumstances , it would be indelicate in us to hint at Utterly untrue But why Mr . Vivian Grey should deem the fact of such overtures having been made ' impossible ,' I confess , astonishes me Impossible , my Lord Ay , Mr . Grey , impossible , that was your word Oh , my Lord ! what should I know about these matters Nay , nay , Mr .
