# text = To say the truth , we are a little rough ; our mane wants pulling and our hoofs trimming , but we jog along without performing either operation ; and , by dint of rattling the whip against the splash-board , using all one's persuasion of hand and voice , and jerking the bit in his mouth , we do contrive to get into the circuit town , usually , just about the time that the sheriff and his _posse comitatus_ are starting to meet my Lord the King's Justice : and that is the worst of it ; for their horses are prancing and pawing coursers just out of the stable , sleek skins and smart drivers .
