# text = I have stood over the bier of the departed ; I have mingled my tears with those of the sorrowing widower , his young and tender child was on my knee , and as I kissed his innocent lips , me thought it was but my duty to the departed to save the father from his mother's rival Yes , yes , yes It was then , even then , in the hour of his desolation , that I mentioned your name , that it might the more disgust him ; and while he wept over his virtuous and sainted wife , I dwelt on the vices of his rejected mistress Nay ! do not stop me ; let me tell all . ' Cleveland ,' said I , ' if ever you become the husband of Mrs .
