# text = You all travel now , it appears , to look at mountains and catch cold in spouting trash on lakes by moonlight But , my dear sir although I grant you that the principal advantages of travel must be the opportunity which it affords us of becoming acquainted with human nature , knowledge , of course , chiefly gained where human beings most congregate , great cities , and , as you say , the Courts of Princes ; still , one of its great benefits is , that it enlarges a man's experiences , not only of his fellow-creatures in particular , but of nature in general .
