# text = They were soon , however , roused from their sorrow and their stupor , by receiving a peremptory order to quit the palace : and as they retired from the walls which they had long considered as their own , they had the mortification of meeting crowds of the common people , their slaves and their victims , hurrying with joyful countenances and triumphant looks to the palace of their Prince , in consequence of an energetic proclamation for the redress of grievances , and an earnest promise to decide cases in future without examining the quarterings of the parties , in a week's time the cousins were all adrift .
