# text = Their barbarous apathy astounds the philosophers ; who , in despair , when the people tell them that they are happy and contented , artfully remind them that their happiness depends on the will of a single man ; and that , though the present character of the monarch may guarantee present felicity , still they should think of their children , and not less exert themselves for the insurance of the future .
